<title>SINGAPORE: GK Goh full year net falls 27 pct.</title>
<headline>GK Goh full year net falls 27 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended June 30 1996</p>
<p>	   (in millions of S$ unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		  20.18	vs    27.65</p>
<p>    Group share (cents)	6.09	vs     8.40</p>
<p>    Dividend (cents)	   2.00	vs     2.00</p>
<p>    Special bonus (cents)    2.00	vs     2.00</p>
<p>    Turnover		    56.49	vs    73.06</p>
<p>    Operating profit	  26.08	vs    35.20</p>
<p>    Associates		   3.08	vs     2.96</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		     29.16	vs    38.16</p>
<p>    Tax			    9.08	vs    10.38</p>
<p>    Minority interest	  0.11	vs    (0.13)</p>
<p>Note - Stockbroking company GK Goh Holdings Ltd said the second half did not show as much improvement as it would have liked due to moderate losses incurred by some of its overseas subsidiaries amid lacklustre regional stock markets.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
</text>
